        address bob = address(0x2000);
        vm.deal(bob, 10 ether);
        vm.prank(bob);
        bool ok2 = address(c).call{value: 10 ether}("");
        // The reference should revert on the second call (block.timestamp == pastBlockTime - 1), the mutant accepts it

        // The rule: if the second call succeeded (mutant behavior), the balance would increase, but the reference always reverts.
        // We assert that after the allowed operations, if block.number % 15 != 0, the final balance is exactly 10 ether.
        // In the reference, ok2 is false, so only one call succeeds, balance is 10 ether.
        // In the mutant, ok2 is true, balance becomes 20 ether, and since block.number % 15 != 0, no transfer occurs, breaking the rule.
